    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d498">

                <pb facs="0461" n="345" xml:id="pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/523.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minster to Haiti
                        to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The instructions of your March 8 were informally presented to the Haitian
                    Government today, and I am assured that Haiti will continue to do everything
                    possible to maintain neutrality.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Furniss</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d498-a1.xml" xpointer="d498-a1"/>
